  "description": "MOZJEU crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C100 H88 Dy8 N16 O40 P4,6(C3 H7 N1 O1),4(C2 H3 N1),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.742-3.959 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.92-113.37°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C126H148Dy8N26O49P4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
